-- S23 Maharashtra prose — theur
-- Verdict matrix: 8 go / 1 skip / 3 wait
-- Anchors: Chintamani — 2nd Ashtavinayak in traditional order, Madhavrao I Peshwa died here Nov 18 1772 + samadhi inside complex + wife Ramabai sati on same spot, Peshwa-era continuous worship since 1762, Pune 25km via Hadapsar, Bhima-Mula-Mutha river sangam nearby, chintamani means wish-fulfilling jewel

INSERT INTO destination_months (
  destination_id, month, verdict, score, prose_lead, why_go, why_not
) VALUES
('theur', 1, 'go', 4, 'January at Theur — the second temple in the traditional Ashtavinayak yatra and the closest to Pune at 25km via Hadapsar — runs at clean operational tempo. Chintamani (the wish-fulfilling-jewel form of Ganesha) sits at the Bhima-Mula-Mutha river sangam in a temple complex that has run continuous Peshwa-lineage worship since 1762. The samadhi of Madhavrao I Peshwa (who died of tuberculosis here on 18 November 1772, aged 27, after spending his final months in retreat at the temple) sits in the inner courtyard; his wife Ramabai performed sati on the same spot the following day, commemorated by a separate memorial chhatri. Daytime 15-28C, nights 10-12C. The 25km Pune drive takes 45 minutes via Hadapsar-Loni Kalbhor; this proximity makes Theur the most-visited Ashtavinayak among single-temple day-trippers from Pune. Sankashti Chaturthi early month brings Tuesday pilgrim density. The Bhima-Mula-Mutha sangam runs at clean post-monsoon flow visible from the temple ghat.', 'January 15-28C clean weather. Chintamani at Bhima-Mula-Mutha sangam, Madhavrao Peshwa samadhi (died Nov 18 1772) + Ramabai sati memorial. 25km Pune drive 45 min. Continuous worship since 1762. Sankashti Tuesday density.', NULL),
('theur', 2, 'go', 5, 'February makes Theur a Maghi Ganesh Jayanti centerpiece. The festival — Magh Shukla Chaturthi — falls Wednesday 4 February 2026; as the closest Ashtavinayak to Pune (25km via Hadapsar) and the temple housing the Madhavrao Peshwa samadhi, Theur sees the heaviest single-temple density of the secondary yatra peak. The Chintamani murti receives the pre-dawn maha-abhishek from 4am; palki processions run morning and evening; full puran-poli prasad distribution through the festival day. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 3 February 2026 — the day before Jayanti, compounding pilgrim density. Daytime 17-31C, nights 11-13C. The 25km Pune drive takes 75-90 minutes on festival days through Hadapsar traffic. The Peshwa-lineage Marathi pilgrim community attends the Madhavrao samadhi at full density — the historical anchor of the temple complex pulls dedicated heritage-pilgrim flow beyond the standard yatra. Lodgings book 2 weeks ahead at ₹1,000-2,500 festival rates.', 'Maghi Ganesh Jayanti Feb 4 + Angarki Chaturthi Feb 3 at the closest-to-Pune Ashtavinayak. Pre-dawn maha-abhishek, palki processions, Peshwa-lineage heritage pilgrims at Madhavrao samadhi. Lodgings ₹1,000-2,500.', NULL),
('theur', 3, 'go', 4, 'March at Theur holds clean operational temperature through the first three weeks with Gudi Padwa Thursday 19 March 2026 as the Marathi New Year cultural anchor. Chintamani runs extended morning ritual on Gudi Padwa with the wider Pune Marathi community attending; the proximity to Pune (25km) makes this the easiest Ashtavinayak to incorporate into the day. Daytime 21-34C, nights 15-17C. The Bhima-Mula-Mutha sangam runs at low pre-monsoon flow; the temple ghat clean. The Madhavrao Peshwa samadhi and Ramabai sati memorial draw heritage-pilgrim flow at standard density. Sankashti Chaturthi mid-month. The 25km Pune drive remains 45-60 minutes; combine with Loni Kalbhor MIDC industrial area visits or the Pune-Solapur highway lunch stops on the return leg. By final week the heat ramp starts to bite — mid-day temple courtyard becomes uncomfortable. Last clean-comfort window before April compression.', 'Gudi Padwa Mar 19 — Marathi New Year extended ritual at Chintamani. 21-34C first three weeks. Madhavrao Peshwa samadhi + Ramabai sati memorial heritage flow. 25km Pune drive 45-60 min. Last clean window before April.', NULL),
('theur', 4, 'wait', 3, 'April pushes Theur into heat-compromise territory. Daytime 26-39C on the Pune plateau; the temple courtyard stone holds heat 8am-7pm. The Chintamani darshan compresses to pre-9am and post-5pm windows. The Madhavrao Peshwa samadhi inner-courtyard space holds cooler interior 33-35C through day but the open pradakshina circuit and the Bhima-Mula-Mutha ghat approach become uncomfortable past 10am. The river runs at lowest pre-monsoon flow — the riverbed visible to 15m from the ghat steps. Pilgrim flow thins through month; the 25km Pune drive remains 45 minutes but few committed pilgrims attempt the visit in mid-day heat. Lodgings drop to ₹500-1,200. The committed Peshwa-heritage pilgrim flow shifts to dawn-only Madhavrao samadhi visits. Hadapsar industrial area access and Loni Kalbhor MIDC lunch options remain at standard tempo. Push to October for post-monsoon ideal window.', 'April compresses to pre-9am and post-5pm darshan windows. 26-39C; pradakshina uncomfortable past 10am. River at lowest flow. 25km Pune drive easy but few attempt mid-day heat. Push to October.', 'April runs at fragmented schedule. 26-39C heat compresses Chintamani darshan to dawn and dusk fragments; Madhavrao Peshwa samadhi visits shift to dawn only. The full temple-and-samadhi heritage experience does not happen.'),
('theur', 5, 'skip', 2, 'May is unviable Theur. Daytime 30-42C on the Pune plateau — the year-hottest stretch; the temple stone courtyard hits 50C surface noon and holds heat through midnight. Chintamani darshan continues but the practical pilgrim experience collapses — even the 5am dawn slot opens at 28C. The cool stone interior of the Peshwa-era temple structure holds 33-35C through day; the Madhavrao samadhi chamber slightly cooler at 32C; but the open pradakshina, the Bhima-Mula-Mutha ghat approach, and the broader complex are physically punishing. The river runs at year-low flow. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 5 May 2026 — dedicated pilgrim flow continues at modest density but most yatra-pilgrims skip. The 25km Pune drive is the only practical Ashtavinayak run in May (return same day, dawn slot only). Lodgings drop to ₹500-1,000 deep off-season. Push to October.', NULL, 'May 30-42C — year-hottest Pune plateau stretch. Temple courtyard 50C surface noon. Even 5am dawn slot opens at 28C. Madhavrao Peshwa samadhi chamber slightly cooler at 32C but full temple-and-samadhi experience collapses. Push to October.'),
('theur', 6, 'wait', 3, 'June marks southwest monsoon arrival in Theur. First-week rains break the heat — daytime 22-32C, nights 19-21C. The Bhima-Mula-Mutha sangam starts to swell visibly through month; by final week the temple ghat steps below the courtyard begin to flood. Chintamani darshan continues at standard 5am-10pm schedule — the temple structure sits well above the river bank — but the ghat-approach photography window closes intermittently. The Madhavrao Peshwa samadhi chamber and the Ramabai memorial chhatri remain dry and accessible. The 25km Pune drive can take 60-75 minutes through monsoon delays on the Hadapsar-Loni Kalbhor stretch. Sankashti Chaturthi late month brings modest pilgrim flow. Pilgrim lodging ₹600-1,400 with monsoon discount. Time the visit to morning windows after the previous night rain has cleared; the fresh-green Pune-plateau setting around the temple complex is among the better viewing contexts of the year.', 'June monsoon arrival — 22-32C, fresh-green Pune-plateau setting around Theur. Bhima-Mula-Mutha sangam starts to swell. 25km Pune drive 60-75 min with delays. Madhavrao samadhi accessible.', 'June transition month — Bhima-Mula-Mutha sangam swells, ghat-approach photography intermittent, Hadapsar-Loni Kalbhor drive 60-75 min through monsoon delays. Expect at least one wet darshan stretch.'),
('theur', 7, 'wait', 3, 'July holds monsoon-peak rainfall on the Pune plateau — Theur receives 400-550mm through the month. The Bhima-Mula-Mutha sangam overflows the lower ghat steps reliably; the temple platform remains dry but the ghat approach becomes unusable on heavy-rain days. The Chintamani darshan continues at reduced morning-only schedule on monsoon days. The Madhavrao Peshwa samadhi chamber and the Ramabai memorial remain protected and accessible. The 25km Pune drive takes 75-90 minutes through Hadapsar caution sections. AC-bus packages from Pune drop to ₹300-500 day-trip rates. Sankashti Chaturthi pilgrim flow modest. Lodgings ₹500-1,200 at deep monsoon rates. The temple complex in heavy rain (with the Peshwa-era stone structure surrounded by monsoon-green Pune-plateau terrain) is photographically striking but operationally compromised. Time the visit to morning windows after overnight rain has cleared.', 'July rain-soaked Peshwa-era temple complex visually striking; Bhima sangam overflows lower ghat. Madhavrao samadhi protected. 25km Pune drive 75-90 min through Hadapsar caution. AC-bus ₹300-500. Morning-only darshan reliable.', 'July monsoon peak — Bhima-Mula-Mutha sangam overflows lower ghat steps through month, ghat approach unusable on heavy-rain days. AC-bus services on weather-watch suspension. The reliable yatra experience does not happen.'),
('theur', 8, 'go', 4, 'August at Theur opens with Angarki Chaturthi — Tuesday 4 August 2026 — drawing committed Pune pilgrim flow despite the rain. As the closest Ashtavinayak to Pune (25km), Theur captures the heaviest single-Tuesday density of the monsoon season. Chintamani runs extended ritual schedule for the festival; the temple platform remains dry but the Bhima-Mula-Mutha sangam still overflows the lower ghat. The Madhavrao Peshwa samadhi sees its monthly heritage-pilgrim peak in August around the Angarki day. Daytime 22-31C, humid; rainfall sustained at 300-450mm through month. The 25km Pune drive on Hadapsar takes 60-75 minutes through caution sections. Pilgrim density picks up through final week as the Ganesh Chaturthi build approaches — the September festival is two weeks out. Lodgings rise to ₹600-1,500 from early-month discount. The Theur proximity advantage makes August more viable here than at the distant Ashtavinayak temples.', 'Angarki Chaturthi Tue Aug 4 — Pune-proximity Ashtavinayak captures heaviest monsoon Tuesday flow. Chintamani extended ritual. Madhavrao samadhi monthly heritage peak. 25km Pune drive 60-75 min. Pre-Ganesh-Chaturthi build through final week.', NULL),
('theur', 9, 'go', 5, 'September makes Theur a Ganesh Chaturthi anchor. The festival (Bhadrapada Shukla Chaturthi) falls Saturday 12 September 2026 — the 10-day festival running through Anant Chaturdashi Tuesday 22 September 2026. The 25km Pune proximity makes Theur the heaviest-visited Ashtavinayak during festival window — committed yatris combine Theur into the standard Pune Ganesh Chaturthi public visarjan pilgrimage. Chintamani receives continuous palki processions; special pre-dawn maha-abhishek every morning; full puran-poli and ukadiche-modak prasad distribution. The Madhavrao Peshwa samadhi sees Peshwa-lineage Marathi pilgrim density at year-peak. Daytime 22-30C with monsoon tail rains tapering through first week. The 25km Pune drive takes 2-2.5 hours through festival traffic; private operators run 3-day Ashtavinayak packages with Theur Day 1. Lodgings book 90 days ahead at ₹2,000-4,000 festival rates. The Bhima-Mula-Mutha sangam runs at clean late-monsoon flow with ghat approach restored mid-month.', 'Ganesh Chaturthi Sep 12-22 — Pune-proximity Ashtavinayak at festival saturation. Continuous palki processions, special pre-dawn abhishek, Peshwa-lineage Madhavrao samadhi at year-peak heritage flow. Lodgings ₹2,000-4,000, book 90 days ahead.', NULL),
('theur', 10, 'go', 5, 'October is post-monsoon ideal Theur. The 10-day Ganesh Chaturthi peak has dispersed; through first two weeks the residue continues at strong tempo, then settles into clean operational tempo at the freshest visual context of the year. Daytime 19-32C, nights 16-18C. Bhima-Mula-Mutha sangam at full post-monsoon flow; the temple ghat platform fully restored, the three-river confluence visible from the courtyard at peak photographic clarity. The Chintamani temple complex (with the continuous-worship-since-1762 inner sanctum, the Madhavrao Peshwa samadhi, and the Ramabai sati memorial chhatri all in the same enclosed quadrangle) sits in its cleanest visual presentation. Angarki Chaturthi falls Tuesday 6 October 2026 bringing dedicated pilgrim density. The 25km Pune drive returns to 45-minute standard time. Lodgings ₹700-1,800. Combine with Bhuleshwar 30km for a clean day-trip.', 'Post-monsoon ideal — 19-32C, Bhima-Mula-Mutha three-river sangam at full flow visible from courtyard. Theur temple complex (Chintamani + Madhavrao samadhi + Ramabai memorial) at cleanest visual presentation. Angarki Chaturthi Tue Oct 6.', NULL),
('theur', 11, 'go', 5, 'November is the year-best Theur. The post-monsoon Pune-plateau green holds through first two weeks; daytime 16-30C, nights 12-14C — the sharpest cool weather of the year. Chintamani darshan at full 5am-10pm schedule with light woolens needed for the 5am slot. The Madhavrao Peshwa samadhi and Ramabai sati memorial chhatri sit in their cleanest visual presentation; the Peshwa-era stone structures (the temple sanctum, the inner courtyard, and the samadhi chamber) hold light winter morning hue distinctively. Bhima-Mula-Mutha sangam at clean post-monsoon flow; the temple ghat fully restored. Sankashti Chaturthi mid-month standard density. The 25km Pune drive runs cleanest of the year — 40-45 minutes on weekday mornings. Pilgrim lodgings ₹700-1,800. Pune-escape weekend traffic on Hadapsar-Loni Kalbhor is the only operational caveat — book Sunday-Tuesday for cleanest experience.', 'November year-best — 16-30C, sharpest cool of year. Chintamani + Madhavrao Peshwa samadhi + Ramabai memorial at cleanest visual presentation. Bhima-Mula-Mutha sangam clean. 25km Pune drive 40-45 min, Sun-Tue avoids escape traffic.', NULL),
('theur', 12, 'go', 4, 'December at Theur opens with Angarki Chaturthi — Tuesday 1 December 2026, the auspicious month-opener pulling dedicated Pune pilgrim flow. Chintamani runs full ritual schedule with strong first-week density. Daytime 14-29C, nights 9-11C — year-coolest stretch. Light woolens essential for 5am dawn slot. The Madhavrao Peshwa samadhi and Ramabai sati memorial chhatri sit in the cool dry Pune-plateau setting at clean visual presentation. Bhima-Mula-Mutha sangam at moderate flow. The 25km Pune drive runs heavy weekend traffic through the Pune-tourist-escape season — 15 percent longer through December weekends. Sankashti Chaturthi mid-month standard flow. Pilgrim lodgings rise to ₹800-2,000 at year-end tourist peak. Pune-escape weekenders compete with pilgrim flow on the Hadapsar road; the last week (Dec 25-31) at heaviest density. Book mid-month weekdays for cleanest operational experience.', 'Dec 1 Angarki Chaturthi opens strong. 14-29C year-coolest. Madhavrao samadhi + Ramabai memorial clean visual. Light woolens for 5am slot. Lodgings ₹800-2,000. Book mid-month weekdays to avoid Pune-escape traffic.', NULL)
ON CONFLICT (destination_id, month) DO UPDATE SET
  verdict = EXCLUDED.verdict,
  score = EXCLUDED.score,
  prose_lead = EXCLUDED.prose_lead,
  why_go = EXCLUDED.why_go,
  why_not = EXCLUDED.why_not;
